  "worked_solution": "First, we write the number as a regular fraction:\n\n$$\n10\\,\\frac{5}{8}=\\frac{10\\cdot 8+5}{8}=\\frac{85}{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we flip the numerator and denominator, keeping the sign of the fraction. So the reciprocal of $10\\,\\frac{5}{8}$ is $\\frac{8}{85}.$",
